From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the nested Hash full-clone result

The two assignments in the conditional expression let the original value
overwrite the recursive clone. Assign the result of the conditional once.
This is an upstream-generic correctness fix, not a RISC-V-specific change.

---
 lib/Class/Gomor/Hash.pm | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/Class/Gomor/Hash.pm b/lib/Class/Gomor/Hash.pm
--- a/lib/Class/Gomor/Hash.pm
+++ b/lib/Class/Gomor/Hash.pm
@@ -32,9 +32,8 @@ sub cgFullClone {
    my %new;
    for my $k (keys %$self) {
       my $v = $self->{$k};
-      (ref($v) && UNIVERSAL::isa($v, 'Class::Gomor'))
-         ? $new{$k} = $v->cgFullClone
-         : $new{$k} = $v;
+      $new{$k} = (ref($v) && UNIVERSAL::isa($v, 'Class::Gomor'))
+         ? $v->cgFullClone : $v;
    }
    bless(\%new, $class);
 }
